6961: # them out (an agy or muse member's tree check never sees them), the collab directory is outside
6962: # the tree fingerprint, and .gitignore carries .consult.detached-* (D1).
6963: # Writers (D5): the foreground writes `starting` (no pid) ONCE, before it launches the
6964: # background, never after; from then on only the background writes - its self-report `running`
6965: # {pid, start_time, host} first, the members as they start and finish, `done` {exit, summary} on
6966: # EVERY exit path (D3); `codex-consult.ps1 -Status -Prune` deletes the files of runs that are done
6967: # or died, 7 days after (D6). Readers - -Status, -Wait, codex-findings.ps1 -List, the SessionStart
6968: # hook - judge a record that is not done by its background's liveness (Get-DetachedJudgement, D6);
6969: # a background on another host is never judged (D11).
6970: #
6971: # The record (status_version 1), fields in this order: status_version, id (the guid), id8, task,
6972: # kind (run | panel), state (starting | running | done), exit (null until done), started (the
6973: # foreground's clock), updated, finished, wall_seconds, pid, start_time (the background's: UTC
6974: # round trip), host, budget_sec (D4 - -Wait's default timeout), purpose, reply_name, brief,
6975: # members[{position (the roster position; 1 without a roster), lineage, state (D11: pending |
6976: # running | usable | failed | skipped | killed | blocked | commit_blocked | orphan), outcome (the
6977: # panel's Get-PanelMemberStatus phrase; a single run: its bridge outcome), wall_seconds, n,
6978: # handoff (NN), reply}], summary (the summary block the run printed - a single run: its outcome
6979: # lines up to `events file:`; a panel: its `Panel <id8>: ...` block - else its last error line),
